+# Super FX Integration Pass — Pass 1
+
+## Baseline
+
+`SNESticleRevive-StarFox-FourFix-Source.zip` is the selected baseline. It already contains:
+
+- S-CPU/GSU timestamp synchronization at GSU MMIO and Game Pak RAM accesses;
+- shared-RAM write-buffer draining before CPU access;
+- CPU-side ROM ownership handling through `SCMR.RON` while the GSU is running;
+- CPU-side Game Pak RAM ownership handling through `SCMR.RAN`;
+- bounded deep diagnostics for GSU state and PLOT/RPIX opcodes.
+
+The older `GSU-Sync-Patch` is not reapplied because the selected baseline already includes the synchronization work and later fixes.
+
+## Pass 1 change
+
+Added bounded `SNES_DIAGNOSTICS=2` traces for CPU bus accesses denied by the running GSU:
+
+- `[gsu-bus-cpu-rom]`: CPU ROM read receives the snooze vector while GSU owns ROM;
+- `[gsu-bus-cpu-ram] op=read`: CPU RAM read receives open bus while GSU owns RAM;
+- `[gsu-bus-cpu-ram] op=write`: CPU RAM write is ignored while GSU owns RAM.
+
+Each record includes CPU PC, GSU PBR:PC, SFR, SCMR, scanline and H-master clock. Each trace is capped at 64 records to keep deep logging bounded.
+
+No emulation behavior was intentionally changed in this pass; the new records observe existing arbitration decisions.
+
+## Validation performed
+
+- Rebuilt host GSU regression binaries from this source tree.
+- GSU regression: PASS, 17,960 fuzz-oracle cases, zero failures.
+- Bitplane regression: PASS, 98,304 cases.
+- GSU state round-trip: PASS.
+
+## Not yet validated
+
+- PS2 cross-build of this exact modified source tree was not run in this environment.
+- No new ELF or ISO was produced.
+- No PCSX2 or physical-PS2 runtime test was performed.
+
+The next step is a PS2 build with `SNES_DIAGNOSTICS=2`, then a short Star Fox USA run to capture bus ownership records alongside the existing GSU/PPU traces.
