+# SuperFX Stage 7 — GSU state persistence
+
+## Changes
+
+- Added a pointer-free `SNGSU::State` snapshot for all architectural and transient GSU state used by this implementation: registers, flags, bank/config registers, ROM prefetch, pending RAM write, clock budget/remainder, pipeline, last RAM address, COLOR/POR, both pixel-cache entries, code cache and valid-line mask.
+- Added `SnesStateV2T`, an extension after the existing `SnesStateT` prefix. The old `SnesStateT` layout is not modified.
+- `GetStateSize()` now returns the V2 payload size. The generic SaveState/RestoreState methods accept both the new V2 payload and the old V1 size.
+- V2 restore checks the `GSU2` extension tag, restores the base SNES state first, then restores the GSU and recomputes the shared CPU IRQ line.
+- V1 restore remains supported; because it has no GSU data, the GSU is reset and its live ROM/RAM pointers are reattached to the currently loaded cartridge.
+- Added a host-side GSU state round-trip test.
+
+## Validation
+
+- PS2 cross-build: 173 translation units, 161 OK, 12 warnings, 0 errors.
+- GSU host regression: 17,960 fuzz-oracle cases, zero failures.
+- Bitplane regression: 98,304 cases, passed.
+- GSU snapshot round-trip: passed (registers, GO, SCMR and SFR checked).
+
+## Limitations — not a complete SuperFX implementation
+
+This stage closes save-state persistence only. It does not complete cycle-accurate ROM/RAM bus WAIT behavior, per-instruction timing validation, complete BRAMR/backup-RAM hardware, or differential testing of all GSU opcodes against hardware/reference test ROMs. No Star Fox gameplay validation was performed for this build. The previous Stage 5/6 ROM bus trap must still be tested on PCSX2 before any claim of a gameplay fix.
