+# SuperFX Sync Stage 3 — 2026-11-23
+
+## Alterações
+- Added SnesSystem::SyncGSUTo/SyncGSU, driven by SNCPU_COUNTER_LINE.
+- GSU MMIO reads/writes synchronize the GSU to the S-CPU's current scanline clock before observing or changing registers.
+- SuperFX Game Pak RAM mappings now use ReadSRAM/WriteSRAM traps even for aligned banks; these synchronize GSU and apply SCMR.RAN ownership (open bus on denied reads; writes ignored).
+- Replaced per-slice discarded instruction overshoot with a persistent signed GSU cycle budget, preventing clock drift between sync points.
+- End-of-line scheduling now advances only the unconsumed remainder of the scanline.
+- Build configured with SNES_DIAGNOSTICS=2 for deep GSU/PPU counters.
+
+## Verification
+- PS2 ELF cross-build succeeded (MIPS, N32, stripped ELF 5,412,072 bytes).
+- Host GSU regression: PASS, 17,960 fuzz cases, zero failures.
+- Bitplane regression: PASS, 98,304 cases.
+- ISO9660 structure, SYSTEM.CNF, ELF extent and ROM extent/hash verified.
+- Not yet validated by booting this ISO in PCSX2 or on a physical PS2.
+
+## Remaining synchronization gap
+- S-CPU ROM accesses are still mapped directly to ROM banks. SCMR.RON arbitration (including dummy/snooze reads while the GSU owns ROM) is not yet enforced by the CPU ROM map.
+- GSU execution remains instruction-atomic; this is timestamp synchronization at MMIO and Game Pak RAM access boundaries, not a full bus-cycle event scheduler.
+- Therefore this stage is a targeted synchronization experiment, not a claim of cycle-accurate SuperFX emulation.
